// The loop of Counterexample 9 of Hark et al. (POPL'20), where naive lower induction for weakest
// preexpectations is unsound.  Here k strictly increases, so on the occupation-measure side every
// subinvariant is sound (progress rule) and the fixpoint below is the occupation measure.
nat a;
nat b;
nat k;
a := 1;
b := 0;
k := 0;
while (a > 0) {
  {a := 0} [1/2] {b := b + 1}
  k := k + 1
}
?Ex[b]
